IMPORT prelude

-- Minister for Finance (Incorporation) Act 1959 (Singapore) -- the corporation sole "Minister for Finance": suing it (s 2(2)), its
-- seal (s 2(2)), its powers over property (s 3), how it executes deeds (s 4), statutory vesting of property to and from it (s 5),
-- the Chief Secretary's rights and liabilities (s 6), Gazette proof of who the Minister is (s 7), and the saving of other people's
-- rights (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MFIA1959.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The body carries
-- no amendment annotations; the Legislative History's last entry for this Act is the 2014 Revised Edition (operation 31 May 2014).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0185 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a person or business, the answer is narrow: whom to sue or contract with when the counterparty is
-- the Minister for Finance as a holder of property, how a deed from it must be executed, and when its property moves without a
-- conveyance. The whole operative text (ss 2-8) is encoded; s 1 is the short title.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The content of s 11 of the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 (disapplied by s 4(2)) was not read; the rule here
-- says only WHETHER it is disapplied. Nothing about which property the Corporation in fact holds, or any President's order made
-- under s 5(2) or (3), was retrieved. The Chief Secretary Incorporation Ordinance (Cap. 54, 1955 Revised Edition) was not read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Minister for Finance (Incorporation) Act 1959 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2 -- constitution, suing, seal`

-- s 2(1): "The Minister for the time being charged with the responsibility for finance shall be a body corporate under the name of
-- 'Minister for Finance' (referred to in this Act as the Corporation)."
-- s 2(2): "The Corporation may sue and be sued in its name and shall have perpetual succession and a corporate seal ... and until a
-- seal is provided under this section, a stamp bearing the inscription 'Minister for Finance' may be used as the corporate seal."
--
-- The defendant to a claim about property vested in the Corporation is the Corporation, in its own name, whoever happens to be
-- Minister. A change of Minister does not end it: "perpetual succession".
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the Corporation in the name Minister for Finance`
    `the individual who is Minister personally`

GIVEN `the claim concerns property vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Defendant
DECIDE `the party to sue under s 2(2)` IS
    IF `the claim concerns property vested in the Corporation`
    THEN `the Corporation in the name Minister for Finance`
    ELSE `the individual who is Minister personally`

-- The seal: once a seal is provided, that seal; until then, a stamp inscribed "Minister for Finance".
GIVEN `a seal has been provided` IS A BOOLEAN, `the mark is the provided seal` IS A BOOLEAN, `the mark is a stamp inscribed Minister for Finance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mark serves as the corporate seal` IF
        (`a seal has been provided` AND `the mark is the provided seal`)
    OR  ((NOT `a seal has been provided`) AND `the mark is a stamp inscribed Minister for Finance`)

§§ `3 -- powers over property`

-- s 3: "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, reassign, transfer or otherwise dispose of, or deal with, any movable or
-- immovable property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
--
-- Every listed dealing is with PROPERTY. Lending, borrowing or guaranteeing is not a dealing with property vested in the Corporation,
-- and s 3 does not confer it; whether some other law does is outside this Act.
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `buying land`
    `holding shares`
    `selling a building`
    `leasing out land`
    `mortgaging land`
    `surrendering a lease`
    `assigning a debt owed to it`
    `giving a guarantee for a third party`
    `borrowing money unsecured`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 confers the power` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `giving a guarantee for a third party` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `borrowing money unsecured` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4 -- execution of documents`

-- s 4(1): instruments requiring the seal "shall be sealed with the seal of the Corporation in the presence of the Minister for the time
-- being charged with the responsibility for finance, and the Minister shall sign every such deed ... and such signing shall be
-- sufficient evidence that the seal was duly and properly affixed and that the seal is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
-- s 4(2): "Section 11 of the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 shall not apply to any instrument purporting to be executed under
-- subsection (1)."
--
-- The signer must be the Minister FOR THE TIME BEING: a former Minister's signature does not satisfy s 4(1).
GIVEN `sealed with the corporate seal` IS A BOOLEAN, `sealed in the presence of the current finance Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by the current finance Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is executed as s 4(1) requires` IF
    `sealed with the corporate seal` AND `sealed in the presence of the current finance Minister` AND `signed by the current finance Minister`

GIVEN `the seal is affixed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the finance Minister has signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed and lawful` IF
    `the seal is affixed` AND `the finance Minister has signed`

GIVEN `the instrument purports to be executed under s 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11 of the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 is disapplied` IF
    `the instrument purports to be executed under s 4(1)`

§§ `7 -- proof of who the Minister is`

-- s 7: "A notification in the Gazette that a Minister has been charged with the responsibility for finance shall be conclusive evidence
-- that the Minister has been so charged."
-- Without a notification the Act says nothing about proof; the question is then left to ordinary evidence (an inference).
DECLARE Proof IS ONE OF
    `conclusively proved by the Gazette`
    `to be proved by ordinary evidence`

GIVEN `a Gazette notification names the Minister as charged with finance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Proof
DECIDE `how the Minister's appointment is proved` IS
    IF `a Gazette notification names the Minister as charged with finance`
    THEN `conclusively proved by the Gazette`
    ELSE `to be proved by ordinary evidence`

§§ `5 -- vesting of property`

-- s 5(1): property "which immediately before 3 June 1959 was vested in the Chief Secretary, Colony of Singapore, under the provisions of
-- the Chief Secretary Incorporation Ordinance ... shall, on 3 June 1959 and without any conveyance, assignment or transfer whatever, vest
-- in the Corporation for the like title, estate or interest and on the like tenure and for the like purposes".
GIVEN `vested in the Chief Secretary immediately before 3 June 1959` IS A BOOLEAN, `vested under the Chief Secretary Incorporation Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property vested in the Corporation on 3 June 1959` IF
    `vested in the Chief Secretary immediately before 3 June 1959` AND `vested under the Chief Secretary Incorporation Ordinance`

-- s 5(2): "The President may, by order, vest in the Corporation any property ... for the time being vested in any public officer or
-- authority", which vests "upon the coming into operation of any such order ... without any conveyance, assignment or transfer
-- whatever".
-- s 5(3): the President may by order vest property "for the time being vested in the Corporation" in "any public officer or authority".
-- Neither subsection reaches property held by a private person; s 8 saves that person's rights.
DECLARE Holder IS ONE OF
    `the Corporation`
    `a public officer or authority`
    `a private person`

DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `no order`
    `an order vesting in the Corporation`
    `an order vesting in a public officer or authority`

GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder, `the order` IS AN Order, `the order is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Holder
DECIDE `who holds the property after s 5(2) and (3)` IS
    IF NOT `the order is in operation`
    THEN `the holder`
    ELSE IF (`the order` EQUALS `an order vesting in the Corporation`) AND (`the holder` EQUALS `a public officer or authority`)
         THEN `the Corporation`
         ELSE IF (`the order` EQUALS `an order vesting in a public officer or authority`) AND (`the holder` EQUALS `the Corporation`)
              THEN `a public officer or authority`
              ELSE `the holder`

-- "the like title, estate or interest and on the like tenure and for the like purposes": the estate passes unchanged. A leasehold stays
-- a leasehold of the same unexpired term.
GIVEN `years left on the lease before vesting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `years left on the lease after statutory vesting` IS `years left on the lease before vesting`

GIVEN `the transfer is a statutory vesting under s 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a conveyance, assignment or transfer document is needed under the Act` IF
    NOT `the transfer is a statutory vesting under s 5`

§§ `6 -- rights and liabilities of the Chief Secretary`

-- s 6: "All rights and liabilities which were, immediately before 3 June 1959, vested in or imposed on the Chief Secretary ... by virtue
-- of the Chief Secretary Incorporation Ordinance ... or otherwise shall, on 3 June 1959, be vested in or imposed on the Corporation."
-- "or otherwise": unlike s 5(1), the source of the right or liability does not matter.
GIVEN `the liability lay on the Chief Secretary immediately before 3 June 1959` IS A BOOLEAN, `the liability arose under the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation bears the liability under s 6` IF
    `the liability lay on the Chief Secretary immediately before 3 June 1959`

§§ `8 -- saving`

-- s 8: "Nothing in this Act shall affect the rights of the Government or of any bodies politic or corporate or other persons except
-- such as are mentioned in this Act and those claiming by, from or under them."
-- A tenant of land moved by a s 5 order claims "under" the public officer or authority (or the Corporation) named in it, so the
-- saving does not protect the tenant from the change of landlord, though s 5 keeps "the like tenure". The Government is not one of
-- "such as are mentioned in this Act" in the operative sections (an inference: it appears only in s 8 itself).
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the Chief Secretary`
    `a public officer or authority named in a vesting order`
    `the Corporation`
    `a person claiming under the Chief Secretary`
    `the Government`
    `a private landowner`
    `a tenant of land vested by a s 5 order`
    `a company with no claim through anyone named in the Act`

GIVEN `the party` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act may affect the party's rights` IF
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `the Government` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private landowner` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a company with no claim through anyone named in the Act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
